Cluster Insights:
=>Customers in Cluster 0 have lower flight activity and fewer bonus miles, representing low-engagement customers.
=>Customers in Cluster 1 have higher flight transactions and bonus miles, indicating loyal and frequent travelers.
=>Customers in Cluster 2 show moderate airline usage and balanced customer behavior.

PCA Insights:
=>PCA reduced dimensionality while retaining 95% variance.
=>Clustering performance after PCA remained similar to the original dataset.
=>PCA helped improve visualization and reduced feature complexity.

K-Means vs DBSCAN:
=>K-Means formed clear clusters with a good silhouette score.
=>DBSCAN identified dense regions and noise points.
=>K-Means performed better for this dataset because customer groups were more spherical and evenly distributed.

Conclusion:
Data preprocessing and scaling improved clustering performance.K-Means provided better cluster separation compared to DBSCAN.PCA helped reduce dimensions without major information loss.Customer segmentation can help airlines identify loyal and low-engagement customers for targeted marketing strategies.
